From 905dc0065dae7655dc46e886eddf7b80f5f3c8d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:00:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] mm/nommu: allow regions that start at the same address
To: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>,
    "Liam R. Howlett" <liam@infradead.org>,
    Vlastimil Babka <vbabka@kernel.org>,
    David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>,
    Jann Horn <jannh@google.com>,
    Pedro Falcato <pfalcato@suse.de>,
    Mike Rapoport <rppt@kernel.org>,
    Greg Ungerer <gerg@linux-m68k.org>,
    linux-mm@kvack.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

add_nommu_region() orders the global region tree by start address and
calls BUG() when a different region already starts at the same address.
Direct mappings of character devices can overlap other regions (see the
comment above the search for shareable regions in do_mmap()), so the
case is reachable from userspace: a /dev/mem mapping of the physical
page that backs another process's anonymous mapping panics the kernel:

  kernel BUG at mm/nommu.c:490!
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt

The tree is only walked in order, by do_mmap() in the search for
shareable regions of a file and by /proc/maps, and both walks are
correct when start addresses are equal. Order regions with equal starts
by the address of their struct vm_region.

Reproduced on QEMU's riscv64 virt machine with nommu_virt_defconfig plus
CONFIG_DEVMEM=y and CONFIG_STRICT_DEVMEM=n, on top of the previous
patch, which makes /dev/mem mappable on NOMMU again. With this patch the
/dev/mem mapping succeeds, and reading it gives the other process's
data.

Fixes: 8feae13110d6 ("NOMMU: Make VMAs per MM as for MMU-mode linux")
Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
---
 mm/nommu.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/nommu.c b/mm/nommu.c
index 23a36fcc40..605cc4021a 100644
--- a/mm/nommu.c
+++ b/mm/nommu.c
@@ -486,8 +486,11 @@ static void add_nommu_region(struct vm_region *region)
 			p = &(*p)->rb_right;
 		else if (pregion == region)
 			return;
+		/* Direct device mappings may alias another region's start. */
+		else if (region < pregion)
+			p = &(*p)->rb_left;
 		else
-			BUG();
+			p = &(*p)->rb_right;
 	}
 
 	rb_link_node(&region->vm_rb, parent, p);
